# Data

## Manuscript raw IQ data (`fluxonium1/`, `transmon/`)

These directories contain the raw experimental IQ datasets for the full
readout-duration sweeps of the main-text figures listed below. Each run
folder holds two files, copied byte for byte from the lab NAS (SHA-256
checked against the source):

- `data.ddh5`, the original measurement file;
- `param_dict.json`, the measurement parameters.

Nothing is thresholded, converted or reduced. The folder names are the
original run names.

| Figure | Device | Measurement | Source run(s) | Public file(s) | Sweep |
|--------|--------|-------------|---------------|----------------|-------|
| Fig. 3(a) | Fluxonium 1 | assignment / bit flip, I sequence | 32504 (\|g⟩), 32505 (\|e⟩) | `fluxonium1/32504-…/data.ddh5`, `fluxonium1/32505-…/data.ddh5` | full t_RO sweep, 2–20 µs (19 points) |
| Fig. 3(b) | Transmon | assignment / bit flip, I sequence | 03664 (\|g⟩), 03665 (\|e⟩) | `transmon/03664-…/data.ddh5`, `transmon/03665-…/data.ddh5` | full t_RO sweep, 0.25–10.15 µs (40 points) |
| Fig. 4(c) | Transmon | long-lived leakage, all-X (+ I references) | 03663 (+ 03664, 03665) | `transmon/03663-…/data.ddh5` (+ the two files above) | full t_RO sweep, 0.25–10.15 µs (40 points) |
| Fig. 4(e) | Fluxonium 1 | short-lived leakage, X-τ-X + I reference | 32501 (\|g⟩), 32502 (\|e⟩) + 32504, 32505 | `fluxonium1/32501-…/data.ddh5`, `fluxonium1/32502-…/data.ddh5` (+ the Fig. 3(a) files) | full t_RO sweep, 2–20 µs (19 points) |

Each I-sequence dataset is stored once, even when two figures use it:

- 32504 and 32505 are used by Fig. 3(a) and Fig. 4(e);
- 03664 and 03665 are used by Fig. 3(b) and Fig. 4(c).

Fig. 4(f) (the τ sweep) is **not** included.

### Common file layout

Each `data.ddh5` file (plottr/labcore DDH5, read with `red.load_ddh5`) has
an HDF5 group `data` containing:

- `data`: the repeated-readout IQ, shape `(n_tRO, n_runs, n_cycles)`;
- `ground_data`, `excited_data` (and `f_data` for the transmon): the
  single-shot calibration IQ at every sweep point, shape `(n_tRO, n_cal)`;
- `gate_seq`: the gate before each readout, 0 = I, 1 = X, shape
  `(n_tRO, n_cycles)`;
- the sweep axis: `sweep_param1` (Fluxonium 1) or `sweep_param` (transmon),
  the readout duration in seconds.

### Fluxonium 1 (`fluxonium1/`, acquired 2026-05-05)

Each file: `data` is complex64 `(19, 8192, 50)`, with calibration complex128
`(19, 8192)`. The sweep `sweep_param1` runs from 2 to 20 µs in 1 µs steps
(index k ↔ t_RO = k + 2 µs).

| Run | Sequence | Stored `gate_seq` | Physical branch | Contributes to | Shared |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 32504 | I | X, I, I, … | \|g⟩ | ε_a = P(S2), ε_bf = P(S1); I reference for ε_sl | Fig. 3(a), Fig. 4(e) |
| 32505 | I | I, I, I, … | \|e⟩ | ε_a = P(S2), ε_bf = P(S1); I reference for ε_sl | Fig. 3(a), Fig. 4(e) |
| 32501 | X-τ-X, τ = 1.5 µs | X, I, I, … (net gate; the X-τ-X pair is an identity) | \|g⟩ | P(S1 \| X-τ-X) for ε_sl = P(S1\|X-τ-X) − P(S1\|I) | Fig. 4(e) only |
| 32502 | X-τ-X, τ = 1.5 µs | I, I, I, … | \|e⟩ | as above | Fig. 4(e) only |

**Branch mapping (important).** The stored calibration field names are
*inverted* relative to the physical labels used in the paper:

| Stored field | Physical state |
|---|---|
| `ground_data` | \|e⟩ (the state left by reset) |
| `excited_data` | \|g⟩ |

So the qubit starts in physical |e⟩ (`initial_state = 1` in the package):

- the I runs without an X (32505, 32502) are the |e⟩ branch;
